# ============================================================
# LOADING SYSTEM
# ============================================================


CornUi supports loadstring execution.

Example:

```lua
local CornUi = loadstring(
    game:HttpGet(
        "URL"
    )
)()
Do NOT assume:
require(game.ReplicatedStorage.CornUi)
is always available.
All code must support:
loadstring environments
Roblox ModuleScript environments
executor environments
Avoid:
Studio-only APIs
plugin-only features
filesystem assumptions
============================================================
INIT SYSTEM
============================================================
init.lua is the public API entry.
Current init.lua:
local Library =
	require(script.Core.Library)


Library.Window =
	require(script.Window.Window)


Library.Widgets =
	require(script.Widgets)


Library.Config =
	require(script.Core.Config)


Library.ThemeManager =
	require(script.Core.ThemeManager)


return Library
Do NOT manually register widgets inside init.lua.
Widgets are handled by:
Source/Widgets/init.lua
============================================================
LIBRARY SYSTEM
============================================================
Core.Library.lua contains global CornUi state.
It manages:
Library.Windows
Active windows
Library.Flags
Global flags
Library.Configs
Saved configs
Library.Plugins
Plugin registry
Library.Themes
Theme registry
Library._registry
Internal objects:
Windows
Widgets
Notifications
Commands
Always use:
Library:RegisterWindow()
Library:RegisterWidget()
Library:RegisterCommand()
instead of manually inserting objects.
============================================================
WINDOW SYSTEM
============================================================
Window.lua creates UI windows.
Window object stores:
self.Name
self.Subtitle
self.Icon
self.Theme
self.Tabs
self.Widgets
self.Notifications
self.Commands
Windows must:
Create ScreenGui
Create Main frame
Create Tab holder
Create Page holder
Attach Tabs system
Attach Methods
Register with Library
Never bypass:
Library:RegisterWindow(self)
============================================================
WIDGET SYSTEM
============================================================
Widgets are stored in:
Source/Widgets/
The widget registry is:
Source/Widgets/init.lua
Currently supported widgets:
Button
Toggle
Slider
Dropdown
ColorPicker
Keybind
Label
Section
Divider
Paragraph
Image
ProgressBar
Notification
New widgets MUST:
Be modular
Return their widget object
Support Destroy()
Support configuration tables
Register with State if applicable
============================================================
WIDGET STYLE
============================================================
Preferred pattern:
local Widget = {}

Widget.__index = Widget


function Widget.new(parent, config)

end


function Widget:Destroy()

end


return Widget
For older Create-style widgets:
Widget:Create(Tab, config)
Maintain compatibility.
Do not randomly convert all widgets unless requested.
============================================================
THEME SYSTEM
============================================================
Theme handling is done through:
Core.ThemeManager
Never hardcode colors when possible.
Avoid:
Color3.fromRGB(...)
Prefer:
ThemeManager:GetColor("Element")
ThemeManager:GetColor("Background")
ThemeManager:GetColor("Text")
ThemeManager:GetColor("Accent")
Themes should support:
Dark
Light
Custom themes
============================================================
CONFIG SYSTEM
============================================================
Config.lua handles:
Flags
Saving
Loading
Exporting
Importing
Use:
Config:SetFlag()
Config:GetFlag()
Config:Export()
Config:Import()
Do not create duplicate flag systems.
============================================================
STATE SYSTEM
============================================================
State.lua manages runtime objects.
Contains:
Windows
Widgets
Plugins
Flags
Notifications
Use State for:
tracking
cleanup
global runtime data
Avoid duplicating State logic.
============================================================
SIGNAL SYSTEM
============================================================
Signal.lua provides internal events.
Existing events:
ThemeChanged
WindowCreated
WindowDestroyed
WidgetCreated
ConfigChanged
PluginLoaded
PluginUnloaded
NotificationCreated
Use Signals for internal communication.
Avoid direct dependency chains.
============================================================
CODING RULES
============================================================
Language:
Luau
Style:
PascalCase modules
camelCase variables
clear naming
comments for major sections
Example:
GOOD:
local ThemeManager =
	require(script.Parent.ThemeManager)
BAD:
local tm=require(x)
Keep formatting readable.
============================================================
SECURITY / SAFETY
============================================================
Always use pcall for:
Plugin loading
User callbacks
External execution
Example:
local success,err =
	pcall(
		callback
	)
Never allow a broken plugin to crash CornUi.
============================================================
PLUGIN SYSTEM
============================================================
Plugins are external extensions.
Plugins may add:
Widgets
Commands
Themes
Utilities
Plugin loading must be sandboxed.
Use:
pcall()
Never trust plugin code.
============================================================
DO NOT DO
============================================================
DO NOT:
Rewrite architecture without asking
Remove backwards compatibility
Delete old APIs
Rename public functions randomly
Hardcode paths
Assume Studio-only execution
Replace modules with single huge files
Add dependencies without approval
============================================================
